cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Koryu attestation log"
message: >-
  If you reference this log, or any figure whose provenance it establishes,
  please cite it as below.
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Shishin Research"
    website: "https://koryu.io"
abstract: >-
  A public, tamper-evident, timestamped record of Koryu's daily crypto
  measurement: the momentum board, the regime dial, and the short board, as
  published at koryu.io. Each day is committed as a chained SHA-256 hash and
  anchored to the Bitcoin blockchain via OpenTimestamps at commit time, then
  revealed in full, so any third party can confirm that a published board
  existed unaltered at the committed time and has not been edited since. Koryu
  is the crypto sibling of Shishin Research. The data (chain/, reveals/) is
  CC BY 4.0; the included verifier (verify.py, standard library only) is MIT
  so that anyone can build an independent checker.
url: "https://github.com/Azoq/koryu-attestation"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Azoq/koryu-attestation"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - MIT
date-released: 2026-07-13
keywords:
  - attestation
  - commit-reveal
  - opentimestamps
  - crypto market measurement
  - reproducibility
